      "id": 1,
      "text": "Sullivan got its name when the Frisco railroad named the station after Stephen Sullivan, leading the post office to adopt the name in 1859.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.theroute-66.com/sullivan.html",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first post office opened in 1856 as Mount Helicon, a mythical Greek mountain, but it was renamed Sullivan after three years.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.theroute-66.com/sullivan.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sullivan’s Harney Summer Home was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1984, preserving a piece of the region’s pioneer history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
